      I've decided to call this a "Yet Another Barely Ascended Post"
for exactly that reason.  This was my second ascension, the first being
a lawful valkyrie.  This one was a weaponless (mostly) neutral monk,
although he ascended by sacrificing the amulet at a chaotic altar.
Things went smoothly enough for most of the game, and then things
started going terribly wrong a little at a time.

      After my first ascension, I played around with the other
tradition 'easy' classes (barbarian, wizard, etc), and got fairly
frustrated and very bored.  To help make things more interesting for
myself, I decided to play a few games with conducts.  I decided to go
for weaponless vegan for a while, and the most obvious choice for that
is a monk.  I enjoyed it so much, that I kept playing them.

      This particular game started like most others.  I hid behind my
pet, steadily raising skill in martial arts until Minetown.  I did the
normal Minetown drill, and ended up getting a magic lamp from Izchak
(and in the excitement forgot to check the number of candles).  I
quickly blessed a holy water at the coaligned temple and wished up the
blessed greased fixed Eye of the Aethiopica.  I left the mines and
completed sokoban for the amulet of reflection, and set up a stash on
the first level of soko (I could branchport back and forth to it with
the eye).  A little above soko, I ran into a poly trap.  It's very rare
that I still have my starting pet by the time I see poly traps, but I
did this time, and I displaced my housecat onto it until he became a
balrog.  After consulting with the people in #nethack, I decided that
he was too slow.  I zapped him with a wand of speed monster and was
still unimpressed.  Before I started using the trap on him some more I
decided to check a hardware store on the level directly above me for a
magic whistle, and lo and behold, it had one.  I named my new pal Benny
and pushed my way up to Medusa.  Between the trap and Medusa, I
accidentally broke vegan conduct by eating a troll to get rid of it.  I
also found a bones pile with a GDSM and a cloak of MR, but those were
useless.  What I enjoyed was the spellbook of idetify (which I soon got
to 0% failure).  Benny dealt with the Titan trivially (by now he was
level 24), and I dug down to the castle.  This where I first got
slapped in the face by Muphey's Law.  I escorted Benny up the stairs,
and then had a thought: "Does Medusa stone pets?"  By then it was too
late ("Benny is turned to stone!").  Medusa then stoned herself on my
amulet, but I was devastated.  I didn't have a stone-to-flesh spell to
bring him back, either.  I was planning on letting Benny clear the
castle for me, but that plan now meant squat.  I broke Perseus' and
uncursed his boots, and then I was on my way.  I dove deeper, deciding
to take a look at the castle situation before trying to get another
pet.  Clearing it the traditional way was out of the question.  I had 0
AC and only ~90 max HP.  On the level before the castle, I encountered
a cockatrice.  I killed him without any thought, but was intrigued when
he left a corpse.  I picked it up (didnt wield it yet.  I've had my
fair share of pit-related trice deaths), and climbed.  I put on the lev
boots from Perseus, and went through to the back door, stoning any sea
monsters that challenged me.  I then went to the square next to the
doorway and kicked it open.  I occasionally encountered an acidic
monster and had to beat it to death with my hands, but they were few
and farspread.  when all was said and done, about 70 statues were all
packed into one doorway.  I locked the door that lead to one room of
soldiers that never got out somehow, and found the wand.  I
branchported to soko and started wishing.

      Since charging was identified, my first order of business was of
course a blessed magic marker.  I know everyone says to wish for
uncursed, because then you can write cursed if you need to, but I wasnt
planning on writing anything cursed with this.  I wrote up 2 blessed
charging scrolls (one for the wand, one for the marker itself).  I then
got myself a blessed greased fixed +2 Helm of Brilliance, the blessed
greased fixed Orb of Fate (risked a 33% chance of failure), some
blessed reased fixed +3 speed boots, and blessed greased fixed +0
gauntlets of power (wished for +3).  I wrote up an assload of blessed
enchant armor scrolls and went to work on my armor.  I got myself down
to -20 AC (inculding protection from here and there).  I thought about
using my last wish on a ring of conflict, but instead got another
marker to write up some genocides.

      I messed around in Gehennom for a bit, smoked Asmodeus, and got
down to Baalzebub.  Murphy's law stuck again.  I have a strategy for
demon lords.  I hit them until the teleport to the upstairs on their
level, then I stand on the downstairs and wait for them.  When they
appear next to me, I go down, and I can stand on the upstairs of that
level and beat them to death.  I did this with Baalzebub, and guess
who's lair is the next level down?  Jubilex decided to help his buddy
out.  One of them, I still don't know who, summoned Yeenoghu to the
party soon after.  I did the wand of digging trick to Jubilex, and
Yeenoghu shot him with a wand of magic missile which killed him.  I
believe it was then Yeenoghu who summoned Juby's replacement:
Demogorgon.  I was flabbergasted by then.  I barely kept alive with my
unicorn horn as Demo made me repeatedly ill.  As soon as I got a turn
where I asnt inches from death, I engraved Elbereth with a wand of
fire.  I then kept doing that on several squares until I was standing
on the upstairs of Jubilex's level on a burned Elbereth.  I then beat
Demogorgon to death from that (but not after he got me sick and nearly
killed me again.  I repeated the process with Baalzebub, but he read a
ursed teleport scroll at the last minute, and by then he could have
been anywhere.  Yeenoghu was the last to go.  I then proceeded to kill
Orcus, who had one death charge left in his trusty wand.  I decided to
use it on my buddy Kaen.

      I decided it was time for me to finally face off with Kaen.  I
planned on using the speed system to get down the stairs, get in line
with him, and zap him before he woke up (I was invisible and stealthy
at that point).This seemed viable enough until Murphy's Law reminded me
of itself (I was seeing more and more of this painful rule).  I fell
through a trap door and landed in Kaen's lair.  This wasnt bad in
itself, as I still could sneak up on him fairly well with stealth and
invisibility, but Murphy threw me a Xorn with a cursed potion of
invisibility (aggravates monsters) to wake him up before I wanted, and
Kaen visited.  The very first round, he laid out 30 damage before I
even had a chance to react.  I stopped myself and reviewed my inventory
several times.  What I then did was looked at my spell list.  Right on
top was a friendly-looking "sleep".  I spammed sleep on him and
proceeded to wail on him.  He woke up and ported to the stairs with 12
HP left (I was checking with a stethoscope every round).  I chased
after him, casted more sleep, and finally killed him.

      I proceeded to Vlad, who was slain by my uncursed worthless piece
of blue glass.  I went to visit Izchak, who had only 5 candles
(MurphyMurphyMurphy).  I went through the first 20 levels of fountains,
and got no wishes.  I had no means of polymorphing anything, either.
The next thought that went through my mind was "pudding farm."  I found
a nice level with an altar right next to the stairs down.  I dug out a
fairly small area as far as farms go.  I went up, kicked a black
pudding out of a sink, and was at a loss of getting him down to my
farm.  I realized I had a stashed wand of turn undead, and got to work.
 I lured him to the stairs down, killed him, crried the corpse down,
and zapped him.  Rinse and repeat.  Soon, I had several hundred
puddings getting slain and sacrificed.  I got a LOT of spellbooks from
praying, as well as a dropped shield of reflection.  This freed up my
amulet slot for life saving (which was good).  I also got a decent
amount of protection (and then lost it by accidentally praying to
early), and a large amount of HP for my level (250 at level 15).  When
I got a spellbook of polymorph, I branchported to my stash, and
polypiled all my tools until I got 2 candles.  I then went up to
Medusa's, and stone-fleshed poor Benny (remember him?).  We waltzed
back down and killed every pudding still alive in the farm.  I went to
nab the Wizard of Yendor.  Since another spell I'd gotten was charm
monster, I used it.  None of my pets were poerful enough to kill
Rodney, however.  He double troublied himself twice when I met him in
his tower.  I gathered Benny and invoked the orb to get back down to
the VS (which got marked a few thousand turns ago).  I performed the
invokation, and swept through the sanctum with surprising ease.  I
tamed a purple worm while down there, and used a cockatrice corpse
through much of it (those guys always seemed there when I needed them,
in spite of my arch-nemesis Murphy).  I climbed like hell, always
keeping my worm and Benny with me.  I met Rodney not once before
hitting the planes, although my worm got slimed in one if his summon
parties.  Earth was trivial.  Things then got messy.

      Murphey's Law struck like a STORM.  NOTHING went my way.  A lot
of it was my own fault.  I forgot to bring enough scrolls of gold
detection with me.  I used my only one up on earth, and then was forced
to wield the Amulet to find the portal on the plane of air (where Benny
was killed).  I tamed a Titan, which got killed on the plane of fire.
I met FOUR archons there, eventually having to dispatch 2 of them
before I found the portal.  Water was perhaps the worst.  I levitated
around waiting for the Amulet to get warm, and Rodney visited.  He
stole the Amulet, then double troubled himself, and stole the eyes.  I
killed them, and then realized that they dropped both under the water.
A red dragon picked the amulet up somehow, and I killed it, to find the
Amulet under water again.  I waited for a bubble to float over to where
they were, but it was the edge of the screen, so nothing came.  Well,
something came.  Its name was the Wizard of Yendor.

      He visited on the water plane AGAIN, picked up the Amulet, and I
was able to kill him in a bubble, recover the Amulet, and retrieve the
eyes.  I found the protal and went through.  By now, everyone in
#nethack was watching through NAO and yelling at me for being so
retarded.  Everyone had their own opinion about how long it would take
me to die.  I put on a blindfold, and picked Death to be my first
advisary.  I hit the buttons to take the blindfold off, but wait!  "You
can't.  It's cursed."  No biggie.  I hit the buttons to cast remove
curse.  "It invokes nightmarish images in your mind."  Damnit.  can I
pray it off?  I zap a wand of enlightenment "Chih Sung-tzu is angry
with you."  I had NO WAY to uncurse this damn blindfold.  Oh well.  I
had telepathy from praying, and everything on Astral is visible via
that, so along with a map, I could navigate flawlessly.  I never
actually killed Death.  I hit him a few times, and he hit me back, but
a priest casted me a handy meat shield to seperate us.  I got to the
altar (luckily the : command tells you what alignment it is while
blind), and it was lawful.  I decided to take a gamble.  On with the
Helm of Opposite Alignment, which I had no means to uncurse.  I hoped
to see my alignment change to lawful.  I became chaotic.  DAMN.  I died
outside the room to an angel, and lifesaving kicked in.  No more
slip-ups.

      By now my AC is -17 (-10 if I take off my shield to cast).  I go
through to the next altar.  It was technically guarded by Pestilence,
but I avoided him easily.  I tamed a purple worm there, which cleared a
lot of the nasties for me.  I use : on the altar, and guess what?  It's
neutral.  If only I had a way to uncurse mt damn helmet.  I go throgh
to the next wing.  My worm gets killed, and I get cornered in a doorway
between Famine and an angel.  Famine almost killed me.  I dealt the
final hit with less than 30 out of 260 HP.  I dashed through, with
angels hitting me the whole way, and made it to the altar.  I confirmed
it was chaotic and finally offered the damn Amulet.

I'd managed to keep polyselfless and weaponless conduct.  Some of the
#nethack guys sent me mail on Astral, even though I couln't read it
with a cursed blindfold on.

